From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: leave the AP when the station power is switched off

The modem keeps the WLAN firmware powered, but Settings power-off must still
run the normal asynchronous leave sequence. A no-op kept the firmware joined
after the station framework announced link-down and prevented a clean rejoin.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/topaz_sta.c b/bsd/dev/topaz_sta.c
--- a/bsd/dev/topaz_sta.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/topaz_sta.c
@@ -49,9 +49,10 @@ static const uint16_t sta_freqs[] = {
 };
 
 static int
-sta_power(__unused bool on)
+sta_power(bool on)
 {
-	return 0;                               /* the radio stays up with the modem */
+	/* Keep the firmware loaded, but power-off must drop the association. */
+	return on ? 0 : topaz_wlan_leave();
 }
 
 static int
